m","also":"","summary":"One of the sons of Eliab, who joined Korah in the conspiracy against Moses and Aaron.","verses":8,"father":"Eliab","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"dathan_982","name":"Dathan","also":"","summary":"Welled; belonging to a fountain, a son of Eliab, a Reubenite, who joined Korah in his conspiracy, and with his accomplices was swallowed up by an earthquake (Num. 16:1; 26:9; Deut. 11:6; Ps. 106:17).","verses":8,"father":"Eliab","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"ham_1359","name":"Ham","also":"","summary":"Warm, hot, and hence the south; also an Egyptian word meaning “black”, the youngest son of Noah (Gen. 5:32; comp. 9:22, 24).","verses":14,"father":"Noah","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"phinehas_2349","name":"Phinehas","also":"","summary":"Son of Eleazar, the high priest (Ex. 6:25). While yet a youth he distinguished himself at Shittim by his zeal against the immorality into which the Moabites had tempted the people (Num. 25:1-9), and thus “stayed the plague” that had broken out among the people, and by which twenty-four thousand of them perished.","verses":16,"father":"Eleazar","mother":"Daughter of Putiel","v":[30]}],"places":[{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[7,21]},{"id":"red_sea_986","name":"Red sea","kind":"Water","lat":19.0,"lon":39.5,"summary":"The sea so called extends along the west coast of Arabia for about 1,400 miles, and separates Asia from Africa. It is connected with the Indian Ocean, of which it is an arm, by the Strait of Bab-el-Mandeb.","verses":26,"v":[7,9,22]},{"id":"horeb_576","name":"Horeb","kind":"Church","lat":28.58771,"lon":33.92168,"summary":"Desert or mountain of the dried-up ground, a general name for the whole mountain range of which Sinai was one of the summits (Ex. 3:1; 17:6; 33:6; Ps. 106:19, etc.).","verses":16